Security and scope boundaries
- The Java bridge is not a sandbox, signed approval service, or OS/cloud security boundary. Its local --human-approved flag is an operator attestation only.
- Without Java 21+ or the JAR, existing Python allowlists and approval gates remain active. When a compatible bridge is detected but fails, the local approved diagnostic runner fails closed.
- Ollama is optional and contacted on 127.0.0.1:11434 only by AION's existing model workflows. Downloaded model weights have independent license terms and are not bundled.
- Mocked cloud tests do not establish live AWS/Azure/GCP permissions or behavior. No 1,000+ tenant load test, signed corporate approval workflow, or autonomous enterprise worker pool is certified.
- Passing tests are not a penetration test, security certification, or proof of production readiness.
